{"schema":"reviewgraphen.benchmark.candidate_output.v1","trial_id":"m7-real:snapshot-27:full_review_graphen:2","outcome":"structured","findings":[{"local_id":"predictable-materialization-clobber","locations":[{"path":"rust/fslc/src/main.rs","start_line":46,"end_line":50},{"path":"rust/fslc/src/main.rs","start_line":68,"end_line":78}],"mechanism_tags":["check_write_gap","cross_file_effect","unstable_token"],"rationale":"The PID-derived adjacent path is opened with std::fs::write rather than exclusive creation. A pre-existing file is truncated and later deleted; a pre-positioned symlink can redirect the write to another file. PID reuse also makes collisions with stale materializations possible.","severity":"high"},{"local_id":"reentrant-materialization-alias","locations":[{"path":"rust/fslc/src/main.rs","start_line":46,"end_line":50},{"path":"rust/fslc/src/main.rs","start_line":68,"end_line":78}],"mechanism_tags":["repeatable_entry","repeated_effect","state_transition_gap","unstable_scope_key"],"rationale":"The materialization key contains only the source stem and process ID. Reentrant or concurrent materializations for the same source in one process therefore share a path, and dropping either guard removes the file while another guard may still depend on it.","severity":"medium"}],"obligation_results":[{"packet_id":"context-envelope:sha256:497a9bffb1f6773ea5d4af4f6014e0ee61dac8a735b2b12ee7251015854df613","disposition":"inconclusive","finding_local_ids":[]},{"packet_id":"context-envelope:sha256:4f494bba8f975b7dda62bbd34a69241e404b6163c81acc2be7232abbdca1a4cc","disposition":"inconclusive","finding_local_ids":[]},{"packet_id":"context-envelope:sha256:7012a24e4346b724710763a84b2310819d9ba979e0e1205d1a2066b6a0ca3ac0","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["reentrant-materialization-alias"]},{"packet_id":"context-envelope:sha256:86733eb0be3b2822b9ba09937e2ceb671c243a5e15b6c5f43642daaaa5a3677d","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["reentrant-materi